In article <1992Mar11.200305.7904@pellns.alleg.edu>, binders@carr113.alleg.edu (Simon Binder) writes:
> I need to find a version of Nethack that runs on the NeXT!

     Get the sources, follow the instructions in Install.unix and
configure for BSD Unix.  It will build a terminal-oriented version,
not one that uses the NeXT's windowing software.  There is one minor
gotcha while building, involving yacc or lex processing (I don't
remember which).  The solution to that is to do 
 % touch src/lev*.[ly]
prior to 'make' so that the yacc and lex source files will be newer
than the corresponding pre-processed files included in the distribution.

In article <1992Mar11.122017.1@acad3.alaska.edu>, fsrsg@acad3.alaska.edu (Richard S. Guse) writes...
> Speaking of this, I've run through this whole newsgroup already, and
> am still wondering if there's versions that I can get for vax/vms systems
> running >5.0?

     NetHack can be built under VMS with either VAX C or GNU C, on V4.6
and up, including V5.5.  The FAQ posting mentions where you can find
prebuilt binaries and the sources repackaged in VMS-specific format.
(It only lists the DECnet address for NSI/DECnet [formerly SPAN], but
that same host is accessible over the Internet:  uars.acd.ucar.edu.)
Since 'ACAD3' is connected to NSI/DECnet, you can find the files by
just doing
 $ dir acdurs::sys$lcl:[src.nethack]
and then use 'copy' to retrieve them.  The FAQ posting has the numeric
address for ACDURS:: if it's not defined in your DECnet database.

